# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model weights and training outputs.
# These are REPRODUCIBLE (train.py regenerates them) and huge: runs/ alone is
# 1.4 GB. Git stores every version of a file forever, and a .pt barely
# compresses, so a few commits of a checkpoint would outgrow all the code by
# three orders of magnitude.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
runs/
lora_r8/
lora_r8_posw/
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.safetensors

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# XAI attribution outputs: ~190 MB of .npz per model, ten of them.
# The scripts that produce them ARE tracked, which is what matters.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
xai_lora_*/
xai_dms_*/
xai_pdb/
*.npz
*.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The virtual environment. Never commit one: it is hundreds of MB, specific to
# this machine's Python and CUDA, and useless to anyone else. A
# requirements.txt reproduces it in one line instead.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# No trailing slash on .venv: it is a SYMLINK to ../ESM2Classifier/.venv here,
# and a pattern ending in "/" matches directories only -- a symlink is not one.
.venv
.venv.bak/
venv/
env/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python bytecode: generated from the .py files on every run.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Datasets. Large, and often not ours to redistribute. The build scripts and
# the documented provenance go in the repo; the bytes do not.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.csv
*.fasta
*.pdb
*.h5
*.hdf5
raw/
splits/
classifier_dataset/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Accidental 0-byte FILES created by a shell typo on 25 Sep (np, os, plt,
# torch -- redirections that were meant to be imports). No trailing slash:
# they are files, not directories. Safe to delete outright; ignored here so
# they cannot be committed by accident in the meantime.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/np
/os
/plt
/torch

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Figures. All of them are regenerated by the plotting scripts, which ARE
# tracked: plot_architecture_schemes.py, plot_lora_results.py, xai/plot_xai.py.
# Binary files do not diff and do not compress, so every re-run of a figure
# would add its full size to the history permanently.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.png
*.pdf
*.svg

# ...except results/, which holds the small number of CURATED figures that the
# README and the reports refer to. "!" un-ignores; a later rule beats an earlier
# one, so this has to come after *.png above. Keep this directory hand-picked:
# anything dropped here is committed forever at full size.
!results/
!results/*.png
!results/*.pdf
!results/*.svg

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor, OS and tooling noise.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.claude/
